  "fields": {
    "title": "Spatial Interface",
    "textContent": {
      "nodeType": "document",
      "data": {},
      "content": [
        {
          "nodeType": "heading-3",
          "data": {},
          "content": [
            {
              "nodeType": "text",
              "value": "Description",
              "marks": [],
              "data": {}
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "nodeType": "paragraph",
          "data": {},
          "content": [
            {
              "nodeType": "text",
              "value": "A spatial interface is either a 3D interface in the field of virtual reality and augmented reality or a 2D interface that displays an apparently spatial surface and uses real objects as a metaphor to describe properties and interaction possibilities. These include, for example, the desk or the wastepaper basket of a computer. The real objects and places become part of a spatial interface, which becomes a basic reference system for people through its familiarity. They can orientate themselves through this system and navigate within the interface because they can locate objects and establish environmental references. The origin of this concept lies in the assumption that people have an innate sense of space, which designers can use to make the behaviour of elements inside an interface  predictable and therefore intuitively usable. The concept of spatial interfaces is not only used in the design of ",
              "marks": [],
              "data": {}
            },
            {
              "nodeType": "entry-hyperlink",
              "data": {
                "target": {
                  "sys": {
                    "id": "1DDBuJHPyDiiT0BOAEo8V6",
                    "type": "Link",
                    "linkType": "Entry"
                  }
                }
              },
              "content": [
                {
                  "nodeType": "text",
                  "value": "GUI",
                  "marks": [],
                  "data": {}
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "nodeType": "text",
              "value": "s, but has also been an important guideline for the design of websites since the beginning of the web, especially for the view on mobile devices that are operated by touch.",
              "marks": [],
              "data": {}
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "nodeType": "heading-3",
          "data": {},
          "content": [
            {
              "nodeType": "text",
              "value": "Background",
              "marks": [],
              "data": {}
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "nodeType": "paragraph",
          "data": {},
          "content": [
            {
              "nodeType": "text",
              "value": "The concept of spatial interfaces was already anchored in the first home computers, such as the Apple Macintosh from 1984 or its predecessors at Xerox PARC. ",
              "marks": [],
              "data": {}
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
